Here is a complete, production-grade overhaul for **Hopkins Care Partner Connect (FTD)**.

This guide reorganizes your repository, builds a serious, modular **Node.js 24 + PostgreSQL 16** backend, connects your configuration file, and walks you through deploying it under your server layout:
* `/var/www/ftdcare/html/` (Vite frontend production build)
* `/var/www/ftdcare/app/` (Node.js 24 backend)
* `/var/www/ftdcare/config/ftdcare.env` (Environment variables)

---

### 1. Server Folder Structure

On your server (e.g., at `/var/www/ftdcare`), structure your folders as follows:

```text
/var/www/ftdcare/
├── config/
│   └── ftdcare.env                # Sensitive production credentials
├── html/                          # Static frontend files (Vite build output)
│   ├── index.html
│   └── assets/
└── app/                           # Production backend code
    ├── package.json
    ├── tsconfig.json
    ├── src/
    │   ├── config/
    │   │   ├── env.ts             # Validated env loader
    │   │   └── db.ts              # PostgreSQL 16 connection pool
    │   ├── middleware/
    │   │   ├── auth.ts            # JWT verification & role-based guards
    │   │   ├── rateLimiter.ts     # IP-based rate limiting
    │   │   └── errorHandler.ts    # Centralized error handler
    │   ├── modules/
    │   │   ├── auth/              # Login, register, me
    │   │   ├── posts/             # Moderated knowledge exchange
    │   │   ├── messages/          # Private clinician messaging (Dr. Seema Gulyani)
    │   │   ├── cohorts/           # Regional & subtype support cohorts
    │   │   └── resources/         # Clinician-verified guides & toolkits
    │   ├── db/
    │   │   ├── schema.sql         # Postgres 16 schema & indexes
