### 7. Automated One-Command Deploy Script (`deploy.sh`)

Place this script at `/var/www/ftdcare/deploy.sh` to handle future Git updates cleanly:

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -e

echo "=== Deploying Hopkins Care Partner Connect ==="

REPO_DIR="$HOME/ftd-source"
HTML_DIR="/var/www/ftdcare/html"
APP_DIR="/var/www/ftdcare/app"

# 1. Pull latest git code
if [ ! -d "$REPO_DIR" ]; then
    git clone https://github.com/IsmayilAbdullazada/FTD.git "$REPO_DIR"
fi
cd "$REPO_DIR"
git pull origin main

# 2. Build Frontend and sync to html/
echo "Building Vite frontend..."
npm install
npm run build
rsync -av --delete dist/ "$HTML_DIR/"

# 3. Build Backend and restart systemd service
echo "Building Node.js backend..."
cd "$APP_DIR"
npm install --production=false
npm run build
npm run migrate

echo "Restarting ftdcare.service..."
sudo systemctl restart ftdcare

echo "=== Deployment Complete ==="
```

Make it executable:
```bash
chmod +x /var/www/ftdcare/deploy.sh
```

Now whenever you make changes in GitHub, simply run `./deploy.sh` on your server. It will compile the frontend to `html/`, run any schema updates on PostgreSQL 16, and restart the backend in `app/`.